ck at validation time instead of [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]mid-launch[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]A plan whose provenance header block is malformed is rejected the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]first time anything validates it — `sase plan validate`, `sase plan[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]propose`, and the tale/epic approval gate — with a diagnostic that [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]names the offending section and its line, so an approved epic can [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]never reach `sase bead work` and abort at its archive step; and if [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the archive boundary is ever reached with a malformed document [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]anyway, it fails with that same actionable diagnostic instead of a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]bare `validation:` exception from the Rust binding.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]plan_header_validation.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/plan_header_validation.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-g4[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-g4/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A header-block validity rule in the Rust plan validator[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-diagnostic[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-diagnostic: teach `plan_validate` in sase-core to emit an error [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diagnostic when the document's leading plan-header block does not parse,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]carrying the parser's reason and the offending bullet's line, without [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]touching the plan-header block wire schema; then land it and let [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]release-plz publish the wheel.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Report an invalid header block from `sase plan links validate`[bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]links-parity[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]links-parity: `_link_validation.py` silently skips a plan whose header [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]disposition is INVALID while `plan_links_refresh` reports [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`header-invalid` for the same document; give the validator the same [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]issue so the two commands agree on what a broken header block is.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt the release and pin the rule at every Python validation [bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]surface[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-adopt[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-diagnostic[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-adopt: raise the `sase-core-rs` floor to the release from [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-diagnostic, pin with tests that the new diagnostic fires at `sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan validate`, at the approval gate, and at `sase bead work` before any[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lock or store mutation, and update the `--explain` header-block note [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from advice into a stated rule.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]An actionable failure at the archive boundary[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]archive-guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-adopt[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]archive-guard: `archive_plan_file` projects header sections before it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]validates, so a malformed document escapes as a bare `validation: ...` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ValueError with no path, line, or remedy; make the boundary refuse a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]malformed source before it mutates anything and fail with the diagnostic[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]envelope.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Land the plan-header validation epic[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]land[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-diagnostic, links-parity, core-adopt, archive-guard[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]land: verify the combined tree end to end against a real malformed plan,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]run `just check-full` and `just symvision`, deploy the skill/explain [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]text if it changed, file the collected follow-ups with /sase_new_task, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and close the epic.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-g4","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","phase_bead_id":"sase-g4.1","reasoning_effort":"medium","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-aa356261081b41a2a587d6094ad2aa98","started_at":"2026-08-06T13:08:47.277571+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1786026692,"sha":"d9c13549f9809f2ba8d695027dc7bf76440e7844","subject":"feat(sdd): adopt header-invalid diagnostic and pin it at every validation surface"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"a5c3ccbfe85c0447424368b04024c7eec2583d9b9679cada4bcd251c7537cee4","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-g4.3/chat.md","size_bytes":9123},"commits":{"digest":"04fbb4455a1292ad426b179757becab4cb3707bb8eae2c074061f56cef5b166f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-g4.3/commits.json","size_bytes":259},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-g4.3/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"225a1a3d147c49bd2d970804ad2a26c2bb05118cf87d185deb6e6f4c32c06395","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sas